1
00:00:04,002 --> 00:00:09,957
In this tutorial you will create an experiment, add subjects (participants) and organize their sessions and trials.

2
00:00:10,007 --> 00:00:19,936
When DOCoMETRe starts, choose a workspace: the folder where all your experiments are stored.

3
00:00:19,986 --> 00:00:25,327
Close the Welcome page to reach the Design perspective.

4
00:00:25,377 --> 00:00:30,467
The Experiments view (left) shows the experiments of the workspace as a tree.

5
00:00:30,517 --> 00:00:37,940
The Description view shows the description of the selected item, and the Console view displays messages.

6
00:00:37,990 --> 00:00:43,736
Step 1 - Create an experiment with the 'Experiment' button of the tool bar.

7
00:00:43,786 --> 00:00:49,944
Give it a name and a short description.

8
00:00:49,994 --> 00:00:56,695
Click Finish: the experiment appears in the Experiments view.

9
00:00:56,745 --> 00:00:59,701
Its description is displayed in the Description view.

10
00:00:59,751 --> 00:01:13,044
Step 2 - Select the experiment and click the 'Subject' button to add a participant.

11
00:01:13,094 --> 00:01:24,491
Do the same for each participant of the study.

12
00:01:24,541 --> 00:01:28,497
Subjects are folders of the experiment. The percentage of trials already done will be displayed next to their name.

13
00:01:28,547 --> 00:01:39,931
Step 3 - Select a subject and click the 'Session' button. A session is a set of trials run in sequence.

14
00:01:39,981 --> 00:01:44,348
Choose the number of trials of the session.

15
00:01:44,398 --> 00:01:49,467
Data files names are built from the channel name, plus the session name and the trial number as suffixes...

16
00:01:49,517 --> 00:01:58,981
...and, optionally, a prefix: here the subject code, so that files keep unique names outside DOCoMETRe.

17
00:01:59,031 --> 00:02:03,405
Click Next to organize the session.

18
00:02:03,455 --> 00:02:09,412
This page associates a data acquisition process with each trial. The experiment has no process yet: this will be done in another tutorial.

19
00:02:09,462 --> 00:02:16,674
Click Finish to create the session and its trials.

20
00:02:16,724 --> 00:02:25,945
The session contains 10 trials. [S.Man.] and [V.Man.] mean that each trial is started and validated manually.

21
00:02:25,995 --> 00:02:30,828
Their icon will show whether they have been done or not.

22
00:02:30,878 --> 00:02:47,536
Add a second session to S01 : 'Learning', with 40 trials.

23
00:02:47,586 --> 00:02:54,317
When processes are not needed yet, Finish can be clicked from the first page.

24
00:02:54,367 --> 00:03:06,369
The selected session and its description: everything can be edited later (Edit session in the context menu).

25
00:03:06,419 --> 00:03:12,374
Your experimental protocol is ready: subjects, sessions and trials. Next step: describe the data acquisition system and its processes.

26
00:03:12,424 --> 00:03:18,532
Quit DOCoMETRe with File > Exit DOCoMETRe: the workspace is saved and will be opened again next time.

